 \EvidenceBox{Event decisions and score definitions}{
 \RevisedExcerpt{The additional fixed-rule comparison includes $\tau=0.5$~mm\,h$^{-1}$; no validation-optimized result was saved for that intensity threshold. For the optimized rule, each model's validation predictions define candidates at 300 equally spaced quantile probabilities from 0.5 to 0.999; duplicate candidate values are removed. The candidate maximizing validation CSI is retained, with the first (lowest) candidate retained in a tie, and applied unchanged to test predictions. POD is $\mathrm{TP}/(\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FN})$; FAR is the false alarm ratio $\mathrm{FP}/(\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FP})$, not the false positive rate $\mathrm{FP}/(\mathrm{FP}+\mathrm{TN})$. ROC AUC measures the probability that a randomly chosen observed event receives a higher continuous forecast score than a non-event, with half credit for ties. CSI and AUC are dimensionless. FAR is undefined when no events are forecast and is displayed as a dash, whereas CSI is zero when there are observed events but no forecasts.}
